# Antigravity AI Engine Rules

# Type Safety & Architecture
- Enforce strict, explicit TypeScript compilation typing across all files. No implicit `any` escapes.
- Isolate server file-processing logic from interactive client UI presentation elements.
- Utilize the Next.js App Router layer layout conventions (`/src/app`, `/src/components`, `/src/lib`).

# UI Grid Component Execution
- Optimize data grids to emulate standard Excel spreadsheet behaviors.
- Implement explicit keyboard event handlers (`ArrowUp`, `ArrowDown`, `Enter`) for fast data entry fields.
- Wrap inline style rules cleanly using unified TailwindCSS utilities.
- Context Menus & Portal Overlays: Design floating context structures to match the high-contrast dark terminal color values of the host layout (`bg-neutral-900 border border-neutral-800 p-1.5 shadow-2xl`).
- Dropdown Button Standardization: Force context control items to share uniform utility styles across all columns (`w-full text-left px-3 py-2 text-neutral-300 hover:bg-neutral-800 rounded font-mono text-[11px] font-bold uppercase tracking-wider`).
- Layout Overlay Clean Dismissal: Every context component or popover must hook into a window event listener to clear layout tracking states and close menu popups when a user clicks external coordinates.

# Code Integrity & Output Guidelines
- Provide functional, production-ready code outputs. Never use code blocks containing placeholders or `// TODO` tags.
- Retain all established type interfaces, utility helper functions, and schema definitions during code refactoring cycles.
- Keep structural methods brief, direct, and readable. Avoid overly dense formatting blocks.